exports[`renderDeployPackage：每個目標的檔案（快照） > cloudflare-api > README-DEPLOY.en.md 1`] = `
"# Deployment guide：cinderous-relay（Cloudflare Workers (REST API)）

> Generated by \`cinderous relay build\` (@cinderous/client 0.0.0-test) from \`cinderous.config.json\` (SDK ADR 0050). The config file is the single source of truth: change it, regenerate the package, then deploy — values edited by hand in a dashboard are overwritten by the next deployment.

Other language: [繁體中文](README-DEPLOY.md)

## What this package deploys

- Target：Cloudflare Workers (REST API)
- Endpoint：\`wss://cinderous-relay.<subdomain>.workers.dev\` (replace \`<subdomain>\` with your account's workers.dev subdomain)
- Allowlist：1 public key(s)
- File chunks (vault sync)：off
- Offline retention：7 days
- SDK：embedded in \`sdk/\` (\`file:./sdk\`)（0.0.0-test）

## 1. Prerequisites

- Node.js 20 or newer (\`npx wrangler@4\` downloads wrangler for you)
- A Cloudflare account (the free plan is enough)

## 2. Get credentials

Pick one. **Interactive**: run \`npx wrangler@4 login\`; wrangler opens a browser to sign in (wrangler's own login — Cinderous never handles the credential). **Headless / CI**: create an API token and put it in \`CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN\` in \`.env\`:

1. **Before you start**：You need a Cloudflare account (the free plan is enough). If you don't have one, sign up at https://dash.cloudflare.com/sign-up and verify your email address.
2. **Open the Cloudflare token page**：Open the token page with the permissions pre-filled: https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens?permissionGroupKeys=%5B%7B%22key%22%3A%22workers_scripts%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22edit%22%7D%2C%7B%22key%22%3A%22account_settings%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22read%22%7D%5D&accountId=%2A&zoneId=all&name=Cinderous%20relay%20deploy
3. **Check the pre-filled name and permissions**：Check that these are already filled in: Token name "Cinderous relay deploy"; two Permissions rows: Account → Workers Scripts → Edit and Account → Account Settings → Read. Do not add any other permissions.
4. **Choose the account scope (Account Resources)**：The default is "All accounts". If you have only one account you can leave it. If you have several, we recommend "Include → the account you want to deploy to", so the token can do as little as possible. Leave Zone Resources alone: the relay does not need any zone (domain) permissions.
5. **(Recommended) Set an expiry**：Set TTL to a date very soon (for example, tomorrow). The token is only needed for this one deployment, so letting it expire automatically is safer. Leave Client IP Address Filtering empty.
6. **Review the summary and create**：Click "Continue to summary", check that the summary lists only the two permissions above (Account → Workers Scripts → Edit and Account → Account Settings → Read), then click "Create Token".
7. **Copy the token**：Cloudflare shows the token. It is shown only once; you cannot see it again after leaving the page. Click "Copy".
8. **Save it in .env**：paste the token after \`CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=\` in \`.env\` (\`.env\` is in \`.gitignore\` and never committed).
9. **Delete the token afterwards**：delete it at https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens; create a new one for the next deployment.

If you have several Cloudflare accounts, set \`cloudflare.accountId\` in the config: wrangler reuses the account you last logged into.

## 3. Set secrets

Secrets live **only** in \`.env\` (or your CI's secret variables); the config and the package contain just the variable names (\`{ "$env": "NAME" }\`).

\`\`\`bash
cp .env.example .env
# edit .env and fill in the values from the previous step; .env is in .gitignore
\`\`\`

The relay has no runtime secrets (no \`site.turnKeyId\`); \`.dev.vars.example\` is only a template for \`wrangler dev\`.

## 4. Deploy

The \`cloudflare-api\` target uses the Cloudflare REST API (plugins call \`deployCloudflareRelayViaApi\` in \`@cinderous/client/deploy/cloudflare-api\`, no Node or wrangler needed; from a terminal, \`relay deploy --config\` below also uses REST and needs an API token). You can also use this package's wrangler config; it deploys the same relay:

\`\`\`bash
npm install
set -a; . ./.env; set +a   # load .env into this shell (PowerShell: $env:NAME = "…" for each)
npx wrangler@4 deploy            # bundle only, no upload: add --dry-run
\`\`\`

wrangler creates the Durable Object, uploads, and prints the \`https://…workers.dev\` URL.

One command (when the \`@cinderous/client\` CLI is installed; it reads the same config, maps the secrets and runs the health check):

\`\`\`bash
npx cinderous relay deploy --config cinderous.config.json
\`\`\`

(The \`cloudflare-api\` target uses REST: it needs a Cloudflare API token, not \`wrangler login\`; there is no \`--dry-run\`, so read this package to see the settings first.)

## 5. Health check

\`\`\`bash
curl -fsS https://cinderous-relay.<subdomain>.workers.dev/healthz          # expect: ok
curl -fsS -H 'Accept: application/nostr+json' https://cinderous-relay.<subdomain>.workers.dev/
\`\`\`

The NIP-11 document should show:

- \`name\`：\`Cinderous SDK relay\`
- \`software\`：\`https://github.com/VaalRL/cinderous-sdk\`
- \`version\`：\`0.0.0-test\`
- \`limitation.restricted_writes\`：\`true\`
- \`retention[0].time\`：\`604800\` (seconds)
- \`cinder_accepts_files\`：\`false\`

WebSocket (Node 22+ has a built-in \`WebSocket\`): you should immediately receive \`["AUTH", "<challenge>"]\`:

\`\`\`bash
node -e "const ws = new WebSocket('wss://cinderous-relay.<subdomain>.workers.dev'); ws.onmessage = (e) => { console.log(e.data); ws.close(); }"
\`\`\`

## 6. Roll back

\`\`\`bash
npx wrangler@4 deployments list
npx wrangler@4 rollback            # back to the previous version, or pass a version id
\`\`\`

🔴 **If you changed \`appLanes\`, a rollback does not bring the old DO's data back**: each lane has its own Durable Object; changing the list moves the lane to a new DO, old data is not moved, and rolling back does not reconnect it (it expires with its TTL).
Durable Object migrations are append-only; check before rolling back past a migration.

## 7. Upgrade

1. Upgrade the CLI (\`@cinderous/client\`) and read the ADRs in between (\`cinderous config validate\` lists changes that affect deployment).
2. Regenerate the package:

\`\`\`bash
npx cinderous relay build --config cinderous.config.json --out .
\`\`\`

3. Review the generated changes with \`git diff\` (generated files you edited by hand are refused until you resolve them or pass \`--force\`).
4. Redeploy as in section 4 and confirm in section 5 that \`version\` is the new one.
5. Keep the same \`appLanes\`; \`compatibility_date\` (\`2026-09-01\`) is recorded in the config and never changes with the CLI — change and test it deliberately.

## 8. Cost

Estimate first:

\`\`\`bash
npx cinderous estimate --devices 3 --collaborators 1
\`\`\`

- Cloudflare: Workers and SQLite-backed Durable Objects both have a free plan (https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/pricing/); a personal relay usually stays within it.
- The free plan has 5 GB of SQLite storage per account: set \`site.storageBudgetBytes\` (e.g. 4000000000) so the worst case is checked with \`computeCeilingBudget\` before deploying.

## 9. Security checklist

- [ ] The allowlist holds only your devices and collaborators (\`site.allowedPubkeys\`).
- [ ] \`.env\` is not committed (\`git status\` does not show it); the config holds no tokens (\`cinderous config validate\` checks).
- [ ] The Cloudflare token has only the two permissions, a near expiry, and is deleted after deploying.

## 10. License

- The SDK (@cinderous/client) is **AGPL-3.0-only** (\`LICENSE\`). This package embeds the SDK (\`sdk/\`); see \`SOURCE.md\` for the corresponding source.
- The generated config and glue files (\`wrangler.toml\`, \`docker-compose.yml\`, \`fly.toml\`, \`Dockerfile\`, \`server.mjs\`, \`src/entry.mjs\`, \`.env.example\`, this guide…) are **MIT-0**: change them freely, no attribution needed.
- 🔴 If you **modify the relay program** and let others connect to it, AGPL §13 requires offering them your modified source: point \`site.relaySoftwareUrl\` at it (NIP-11 \`software\`; at most 200 characters). Changing only the configuration does not count.

## 11. Connect to this relay

\`\`\`ts
import { Identity, RelayPool } from '@cinderous/client';

// in a real app, persist the identity with loadOrCreateIdentity
const identity = Identity.generate();
const pool = new RelayPool({ urls: ['wss://cinderous-relay.<subdomain>.workers.dev'], identity });
pool.connect();
\`\`\`

This relay has an allowlist: \`identity.npub\` must be in \`site.allowedPubkeys\` to write.
"
`;

exports[`renderDeployPackage：每個目標的檔案（快照） > cloudflare-api > README-DEPLOY.md 1`] = `
"# 部署說明：cinderous-relay（Cloudflare Workers（REST API））

> 由 \`cinderous relay build\`（@cinderous/client 0.0.0-test）依 \`cinderous.config.json\` 產生（SDK ADR 0050）。設定檔是單一真實來源：要改設定就改它、重新產生部署包，再部署——在儀表板手改的值，下一次部署會被覆寫。

其他語言：[English](README-DEPLOY.en.md)

## 這份部署包

- 目標：Cloudflare Workers（REST API）
- 端點：\`wss://cinderous-relay.<subdomain>.workers.dev\`（\`<subdomain>\` 換成你帳號的 workers.dev 子網域）
- 白名單：1 把公鑰
- 檔案塊（Vault 同步）：關
- 離線留言保存：7 天
- SDK：內嵌在 \`sdk/\`（\`file:./sdk\`）（0.0.0-test）

## 1. 前置工具

- Node.js 20 以上（\`npx wrangler@4\` 會自動下載 wrangler）
- 一個 Cloudflare 帳號（免費方案即可）

## 2. 取得憑證

兩種做法擇一。**互動**：直接執行 \`npx wrangler@4 login\`，由 wrangler 開瀏覽器登入（這是 wrangler 的登入流程，Cinderous 不經手任何憑證）。**無頭／CI**：建立一把 API Token，放進 \`.env\` 的 \`CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN\`：

1. **事前準備**：準備好一個 Cloudflare 帳號（免費方案即可）。還沒有的話，先到 https://dash.cloudflare.com/sign-up 註冊，並完成 email 驗證。
2. **開啟 Cloudflare 的 Token 建立頁**：開啟預填權限的 Token 建立頁：https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens?permissionGroupKeys=%5B%7B%22key%22%3A%22workers_scripts%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22edit%22%7D%2C%7B%22key%22%3A%22account_settings%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22read%22%7D%5D&accountId=%2A&zoneId=all&name=Cinderous%20relay%20deploy
3. **確認預填的名稱與權限**：確認已自動填好：Token 名稱「Cinderous relay deploy」；Permissions 兩列：Account → Workers Scripts → Edit、Account → Account Settings → Read。不要新增其他權限。
4. **選擇帳號範圍（Account Resources）**：預設是「All accounts」。只有一個帳號的話可以不改；有多個帳號時，建議改成「Include → 你要部署的那個帳號」，讓權限範圍最小。Zone Resources 不需要設定：中繼不需要任何網域權限。
5. **（建議）設定到期日**：在 TTL 設一個很近的到期日（例如明天）。這把 Token 只用來部署這一次，到期會自動失效，比較安全。Client IP Address Filtering 留空。
6. **檢查摘要並建立**：按「Continue to summary」，確認摘要裡只有上面兩項權限（Account → Workers Scripts → Edit、Account → Account Settings → Read），再按「Create Token」。
7. **複製 Token**：畫面會顯示 Token。它只會顯示這一次，關掉就看不到了。按「Copy」複製。
8. **存進 .env**：把 Token 貼到 \`.env\` 的 \`CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=\` 後面（\`.env\` 已在 \`.gitignore\`，不會被提交）。
9. **部署完刪除 Token**：到 https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens 刪掉它；下次部署再建一把。

有多個 Cloudflare 帳號時，在設定檔寫 \`cloudflare.accountId\`：wrangler 會沿用上次登入的帳號。

## 3. 設定秘密

秘密**只**放在 \`.env\`（或 CI 的秘密變數），設定檔與部署包裡只有變數名稱（\`{ "$env": "NAME" }\`）。

\`\`\`bash
cp .env.example .env
# 編輯 .env，填入上一步拿到的值；.env 已在 .gitignore
\`\`\`

這座中繼在執行期沒有秘密（沒有設 \`site.turnKeyId\`），\`.dev.vars.example\` 只是給 \`wrangler dev\` 的範本。

## 4. 部署

\`cloudflare-api\` 目標走 Cloudflare REST API（外掛用 \`@cinderous/client/deploy/cloudflare-api\` 的 \`deployCloudflareRelayViaApi\`，不需要 Node 與 wrangler；終端機用下面的 \`relay deploy --config\`，同樣走 REST、一定要有 API Token）。也可以用這個部署包裡的 wrangler 設定，部署出來的是同一座中繼：

\`\`\`bash
npm install
set -a; . ./.env; set +a   # 把 .env 載入這個 shell（PowerShell：逐一 $env:NAME = "…"）
npx wrangler@4 deploy            # 只想先試打包：加 --dry-run
\`\`\`

wrangler 會建立 Durable Object、上傳，並印出 \`https://…workers.dev\` 網址。

一行指令（裝了 \`@cinderous/client\` CLI 時；它讀同一份設定、自己對應秘密、部署後做健康檢查）：

\`\`\`bash
npx cinderous relay deploy --config cinderous.config.json
\`\`\`

（\`cloudflare-api\` 目標走 REST：要有 Cloudflare API Token，不能用 \`wrangler login\`；沒有 \`--dry-run\`，要先看設定就看這個部署包。）

## 5. 健康檢查

\`\`\`bash
curl -fsS https://cinderous-relay.<subdomain>.workers.dev/healthz          # 應該回 ok
curl -fsS -H 'Accept: application/nostr+json' https://cinderous-relay.<subdomain>.workers.dev/
\`\`\`

NIP-11 文件要看到：

- \`name\`：\`Cinderous SDK relay\`
- \`software\`：\`https://github.com/VaalRL/cinderous-sdk\`
- \`version\`：\`0.0.0-test\`
- \`limitation.restricted_writes\`：\`true\`
- \`retention[0].time\`：\`604800\`（秒）
- \`cinder_accepts_files\`：\`false\`

WebSocket（Node 22 以上內建 \`WebSocket\`）：連上應該立刻收到 \`["AUTH", "<challenge>"]\`：

\`\`\`bash
node -e "const ws = new WebSocket('wss://cinderous-relay.<subdomain>.workers.dev'); ws.onmessage = (e) => { console.log(e.data); ws.close(); }"
\`\`\`

## 6. 回滾

\`\`\`bash
npx wrangler@4 deployments list
npx wrangler@4 rollback            # 回到上一版；或在後面加 version id
\`\`\`

🔴 **改了 \`appLanes\`，回滾拿不回舊 DO 的資料**：每條車道各有一顆 Durable Object，改名單＝那條車道換一顆新的 DO，舊 DO 裡的資料不會搬過去，回滾也不會把它們接回來（等 TTL 到期）。
Durable Object 的遷移只會附加（不能刪）；回滾到比遷移更早的版本前先確認。

## 7. 升級

1. 升級 CLI（\`@cinderous/client\`），讀這幾版之間的 ADR（\`cinderous config validate\` 會列出影響部署的變更）。
2. 重新產生部署包：

\`\`\`bash
npx cinderous relay build --config cinderous.config.json --out .
\`\`\`

3. 用 \`git diff\` 看產生的檔案改了什麼（手改過的產生檔案會被擋下，要先處理或加 \`--force\`）。
4. 照第 4 節重新部署，照第 5 節確認 \`version\` 已經是新版。
5. 保持同一份 \`appLanes\`；\`compatibility_date\`（\`2026-09-01\`）記在設定檔裡，不會隨 CLI 改變——要改就自己改、自己測。

## 8. 成本

先試算：

\`\`\`bash
npx cinderous estimate --devices 3 --collaborators 1
\`\`\`

- Cloudflare：Workers 與 SQLite 型 Durable Objects 都有免費方案（https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/pricing/）；個人中繼通常在免費額度內。
- 免費方案的 SQLite 儲存全帳號共 5 GB：建議設 \`site.storageBudgetBytes\`（例如 4000000000），部署前以 \`computeCeilingBudget\` 檢查最壞加總。

## 9. 安全檢查清單

- [ ] 白名單只有你自己的裝置與合作者（\`site.allowedPubkeys\`）。
- [ ] \`.env\` 沒有被提交（\`git status\` 看不到它）；設定檔裡沒有任何 Token（\`cinderous config validate\` 會檢查）。
- [ ] Cloudflare Token 只有兩項權限、設了很近的到期日，部署完就刪掉。

## 10. 授權

- SDK（@cinderous/client）是 **AGPL-3.0-only**（\`LICENSE\`）。這個部署包內嵌了 SDK（\`sdk/\`），對應原始碼見 \`SOURCE.md\`。
- 產生的設定檔與膠水程式（\`wrangler.toml\`、\`docker-compose.yml\`、\`fly.toml\`、\`Dockerfile\`、\`server.mjs\`、\`src/entry.mjs\`、\`.env.example\`、這份說明……）以 **MIT-0** 授權：隨你改、不必署名。
- 🔴 **改過中繼程式**再讓別人連線使用，AGPL §13 要求向這些使用者提供修改後的原始碼：把 \`site.relaySoftwareUrl\` 指向它（NIP-11 \`software\`；最長 200 字）。只改設定、沒改程式不必。

## 11. 連上這座中繼

\`\`\`ts
import { Identity, RelayPool } from '@cinderous/client';

// 正式使用請以 loadOrCreateIdentity 保存身分
const identity = Identity.generate();
const pool = new RelayPool({ urls: ['wss://cinderous-relay.<subdomain>.workers.dev'], identity });
pool.connect();
\`\`\`

這座站有白名單：\`identity.npub\` 要在 \`site.allowedPubkeys\` 裡才能寫入。
"
`;

